<title>MEXICO: Top '95-96 Mexican soybean meal importers listed.</title>
<headline>Top '95-96 Mexican soybean meal importers listed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The local office of American Soybean Association (ASA) listed Monday the top soybean meal importers for the marketing year Oct 1995-Sept 1996. Weight in tonnes.</p>
<p>  Company Name		  Tonnage	    Pct Total</p>
<p>  Jerome Mezoro SA	    169,074	     42.0 pct</p>
<p>  Bachoco SA		    102,161	     25.5 pct</p>
<p>  Alimentos Balanceados	28,357		7.1 pct</p>
<p>  Purina SA			14,667		3.6 pct</p>
<p>  Agroservicios Ragasa	  8,737		2.2 pct</p>
<p>  Agroindustrial Zaragosa     7,611		1.9 pct</p>
<p>  Others			   69,525	     17.4 pct</p>
<p>  Total			   400,132	    100.0 pct</p>
<p>    ASA said the top port of entry was Nuevo Laredo with 40 percent of meal imports, following by Piedras Negras with 25 percent, Ciudad Juarez with 18 percent, Mexicali with 10 percent and Matamoros with six percent.</p>
<p>  --Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
</text>
